{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777965923,"nonce":"UrAXZD+Af6eh5VzezuCyct98TlY=","title":"Phase 10: --ingest v3 -- real UC2 v3 archive output","message":"Builds on v2 (96ef9b8).  Goal: --ingest output is a real UC2 v3 archive that uc2 -x and uc2 -l can list and extract.  Approaches:\n\nA) Each CDC chunk is its own archive entry (synthetic name).  Restore concatenates entries.  Drawback: directory listings are noisy.\nB) Add a new entry type (e.g., 'ingest-stream') that points to a chain of master blocks.  Requires touching compress.c and possibly the cdir format.\nC) Treat the entire stream as a single virtual file, prime LZ77 with the largest CDC chunk as a master block.  No real dedup, just compression boost.\n\n(B) is the most faithful to the v3 vision; (A) is cheapest to ship; (C) is a cop-out.\n\nLikely path: implement (A) first (small change, solves listability), then (B) once the master-block model is better understood.","files":null}]}